    "text": "<p>For the circuit shown, the value of current at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0198_03a390e500cc.png\" style=\"width: 265px; height: 285px;\" /></p><p>[Voltage distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is shown by Fig. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and the circuit is shown in Fig. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From graph voltage at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sec</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>volt</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0198_acdef11bde2e.png\" style=\"width: 232px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>"
